**Definition 4.1 (exact certificate notation).** The tables in §§12–16 use finite records of rational scalars, integer pairs, vectors and matrices. Quoted fractions $n/d$ mean the rational number $n/d$, without an accuracy convention. Source integer pairs are divided by $2^{224}$. All unnamed integer pairs in contact, geometry, polynomial, Taylor, tangent and quantity records are closed interval endpoints divided by $2^{190}$. Explicit rational fractions have their own displayed denominator. An interval tuple with four coefficient pairs means $A+B\vartheta+C\vartheta^2+E$ on the same $\vartheta\in[-1,1]$, with an independent interval remainder $E$. Matrix arrays are ordered by rows. The record notation specifies exact mathematical constants. The complete tables are stored as fixed-version data at the links in §§12–16; the [data manifest](https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing-experiments/blob/08cfceafd9500530ffa128764313472b003a72ab/experiments/theory/fib-native-complete-continuation/connected-interval/manifest.json) records their SHA-256 hashes.

For a cell with `parameter` $[a,b]$, set $m=(a+b)/2$, $h_c=(b-a)/2$, $\lambda=m+h_c\vartheta$. The fields `center`, `slope`, `quadratic`, `radius` specify

$$
X_0(\vartheta)=C+v h_c\vartheta+w h_c^2\vartheta^2,
\qquad \mathcal B_\vartheta=X_0(\vartheta)+\prod_i[-r_i,r_i].
$$

For uniform evaluation the source amplitudes, $\delta,s_0,G$ and $M$ use their supplied rectangles, the enclosed $\beta$ is the source coefficient `beta`, and $\alpha=1-\beta$. At the true source these coincide with Definition 1.4. The field `R` is the exact rational preconditioner; `q` and `inclusion` are enclosing rational upper bounds in the $r$-weighted maximum norm. The field `n` specifies the contact system. In all six-contact cell records the extra stationary coordinate is last. In point records there is no varying $\vartheta$; radius may be a scalar common to all coordinates. The event has radius $10^{-15}$ and the order of Definition 3.2.

For an arc record, `eta`, `epsilon`, `sigma` specify its sheet and two signs, `factors` lists the removed occupied double roots, `quotient` gives interval power coefficients in ascending degree, `quotient_taylor` retains their shared-parameter expansion, and `leaves` gives the full Bernstein partition. A leaf with `left` $j$ and `depth` $d$ is $[j/2^d,(j+1)/2^d]$ in the variable $y=(x+1)/2$; `controls` and `control_taylor` are its interval Bernstein controls and their shared-parameter expansions, in ascending index. The boolean `unused_factor=false` specifies direct certification of the full unused polynomial; when absent in a six-contact cell the unused stationary double division retains its constant gap. Geometry fields specify strict lower margins; `minor_rows` selects the independent moment-column minor and `minor` encloses its determinant. `witness` is the contrast tangent of §6. `saturated_wedges` encloses the pairwise $(z,w)$ determinants. `quantities` gives $s,\tau,\mathcal T_A(s)$ and high/low value expressions with their displayed names. Tangent and point-containment fields have the meanings proved below.

